  "unreadable": [
    "O and 0 look alike in callouts such as TX0/RX0/SDA0/SCL0/CTS0/RTS0 and IO0; recorded as 0 (IO prefix as letters)"
  ],
  "uncertain": [],
  "notes": "Label is the orange RP2040 GPIO box (IOxx) where it names a GPIO; A0-A3 rows show ADCn instead, so the board name A0-A3 is the label. PCB silkscreen first in functions; silkscreen for +3.3V and ARef is partly hidden by components and not recorded. '*' on A4/A5 = digital I/O, not analog, per legend. Battery JST connector (Battery -/+ only), SD card slot and the small Bi2C connector (no pin labels) skipped."
